<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Document types">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/staff-documents/types">Staff Document Types</a> lists the documents you keep for
            staff, such as a DBS check, first aid certificate or right-to-work check. Use <strong>New Document
            Type</strong> to add one, and say whether it <strong>Requires an expiry date</strong>. Deactivate
            types you no longer use.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Uploading a document for someone">
        <ol>
            <li>Open the person from <a href="/manage/users">Users</a> and go to the <strong>Documents</strong> tab.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Upload Document</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Document Type</strong>, set the <strong>Expiry Date</strong> and, if you like, a
                <strong>Reminder Date</strong>, then choose the file.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            On the reminder date, the person is emailed a reminder that the document is due to expire.
            Expired and soon-to-expire documents also appear on <a href="/manage/compliance">Compliance</a>. When
            it's renewed, upload the new copy with its new dates.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Who can see staff documents">
        <FluentText>
            Staff documents are kept private. They never appear in <a href="/files">File Manager</a> and
            can't be downloaded from a kiosk. Only Admins and the person's Managers can see, upload or
            delete them, from the <strong>Documents</strong> tab.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
